# Everything the kit produces locally. None of it belongs in the repo: work/ holds a decompile
# of the game, and port/ holds a built derivative of it.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is not a style choice. `port/` without one matches a
# directory named "port" ANYWHERE in the tree - and on Windows, where git checks out with
# core.ignoreCase, it matches "Port" too. So it silently swallowed
# newfiles/src/UnclaimedWorld/UWGame/Port/, five source files the build cannot do without, and
# every fresh clone of this repo failed in phase 1 with
#
#     error CS0234: The type or namespace name 'Port' does not exist in the namespace 'UWGame'
#
# while the zipped kit, which is not a git checkout, built perfectly. Reported by a modder.
/work/
/port/
/prereqs/
*.log
/orchestrator/uwkit.exe
